me energy left at the end  of a long day  that's where sandbags kettlebells bands  battle ropes and medicine balls come in  or calisthenics and more compound lifts  you don't need any specialist equipment  to get started with functional training  the key is to move in multiple planes of  motion and to use the whole body as one  powerful system  to train the different energy systems to  me fitness relates to all aspects of  human function  a truly functional program should pay  equal attention to strength  endurance mobility balance even  cognitive performance  why not train the brain like you train  the body because imagine what it would  be like to be a little bit stronger  a little bit faster a little more  energetic and a little bit sharper  all at once it's time to find out just  what you're capable of
 

